  "description": "Graphs for coding interviews: representations, grid DFS/BFS, connected components, BFS shortest paths, cycle detection and the bipartite check, Kahn topological sort, union-find, Dijkstra and MST, with tested templates in Go, C++, Java and Python.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">50 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Coding</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Pattern primer</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Graphs</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Graphs: BFS, DFS and the Five Tools Interviewers Expect</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Most graph questions in a coding round are one of five shapes: flood a grid, count pieces, find the fewest steps, order things with dependencies, or detect a cycle. This page gives you one picture, one template and one recognition cue for each, then a short, honest overview of union-find, Dijkstra and minimum spanning trees so you know when to reach for them.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Go deeper:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-graph-bfs\">BFS on grids and implicit graphs</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-topo-sort\">Topological sort</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-union-find\">Union-find (disjoint set union): groups that merge</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-dijkstra\">Weighted shortest paths: Dijkstra, Bellman-Ford, Floyd</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-mst-advanced-graphs\">MST, Bridges and Euler Paths</a>.</p>\r\n"
  },
